{"case_id":"C005","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","API_protocol","configuration","input_semantics"],"confidence":98,"affected_functions":["wuffs_vp8__decoder__initialize","wuffs_vp8__decoder__set_quirk","wuffs_vp8__decoder__get_quirk","wuffs_vp8__decoder__decode_image_config","wuffs_vp8__decoder__workbuf_len","wuffs_vp8__decoder__decode_frame"],"reason":"H0 fuzzes only wuffs_webp__decoder through fuzz_image_decoder. S1 makes the standalone VP8 decoder depend on a caller-supplied base.QUIRK_SOURCE_LENGTH protocol before decode_image_config, with length-derived partition state and work-buffer sizing. The WebP path supplies one internally derived, valid quirk value, so H0 does not directly fuzz missing, malformed, boundary, or source-inconsistent QUIRK_SOURCE_LENGTH values at the public VP8 API.","evidence":["H0 defines WUFFS_CONFIG__MODULE__VP8 but instantiates only wuffs_webp__decoder and upcasts that decoder to wuffs_base__image_decoder.","S1 adds public wuffs_vp8 decoder get_quirk and set_quirk handling for base.QUIRK_SOURCE_LENGTH.","decoder.do_decode_image_config returns #missing QUIRK_SOURCE_LENGTH when the low bit is clear, #bad QUIRK_SOURCE_LENGTH below 10 bytes, and #unsupported QUIRK_SOURCE_LENGTH above 0x08FF_FFF7 + 10.","decoder.do_decode_image_config derives partitioned_data_length from quirk_source_length and validates part_lens[0] against it.","decoder.workbuf_len and decoder.decode_frame derive wb_len from workbuf_yuv_v_end, partitioned_data_length, and 8 trailing bytes; decode_frame then calls copy_partitions_to_workbuf and decode_other_partition_lengths.","The WebP decoder calls this.vp8.set_quirk with ((this.sub_chunk_length as base.u64) << 1) | 1, preventing H0's hash from independently varying the quirk value or its consistency with the VP8 bytes."],"recommended_action":"Add a standalone VP8 harness that initializes wuffs_vp8__decoder, uses fuzz-controlled QUIRK_SOURCE_LENGTH values—including absent/even, below-minimum, maximum-boundary, oversized, and values inconsistent with the supplied bytes—and exercises decode_image_config, workbuf_len, decode_frame_config, and decode_frame with bounded allocation."}
